# Product Specification / PRD

## 1. Product Overview

Code Refactoring Assistant is an AI-powered developer productivity tool that analyzes
source code and provides structured suggestions to improve code quality,
readability, maintainability, and efficiency.

The application currently provides suggestions in four areas:

- Cleaner Code
- Design Patterns
- Optimization
- Naming Improvements

---

## 2. Problem Statement

Developers often spend time manually identifying code quality issues,
improving naming, finding optimization opportunities, and determining
appropriate design patterns.

The Code Refactoring Assistant aims to reduce this effort by providing
AI-powered refactoring suggestions through a simple interface.

---

## 3. Target User

The primary users are:

- Software developers
- Students learning programming
- Developers looking for quick code-quality feedback

---

## 4. User Stories

### US-01: Submit Source Code

As a developer, I want to paste my source code into the application
so that I can receive refactoring suggestions.

### US-02: Analyze Code

As a developer, I want the application to analyze my submitted code
so that I can identify areas for improvement.

### US-03: Improve Code Quality

As a developer, I want suggestions for cleaner code
so that my code becomes easier to read and maintain.

### US-04: Identify Design Patterns

As a developer, I want recommendations for suitable design patterns
so that I can improve the structure of my code.

### US-05: Optimize Code

As a developer, I want optimization suggestions
so that I can identify opportunities to improve efficiency.

### US-06: Improve Naming

As a developer, I want naming suggestions
so that variables and identifiers are clearer and more meaningful.

### US-07: Handle Errors

As a developer, I want to receive an error message when the
refactoring service is unavailable so that I know the analysis failed.

---

# 5. Acceptance Criteria

## US-01: Submit Source Code

- [ ] User can enter source code into the code input area.
- [ ] User can click the Analyze button.
- [ ] Empty code submission is rejected.
- [ ] Submitted code is sent to the backend.

## US-02: Analyze Code

- [ ] Backend accepts the submitted source code.
- [ ] Backend sends the code to the AI service.
- [ ] AI response is returned in structured JSON format.
- [ ] Invalid AI responses are handled appropriately.

## US-03: Improve Code Quality

- [ ] Application displays cleaner-code suggestions.
- [ ] Suggestions are displayed after successful analysis.

## US-04: Identify Design Patterns

- [ ] Application displays design-pattern suggestions.
- [ ] Suggestions are displayed after successful analysis.

## US-05: Optimize Code

- [ ] Application displays optimization suggestions.
- [ ] Suggestions are displayed after successful analysis.

## US-06: Improve Naming

- [ ] Application displays naming-improvement suggestions.
- [ ] Suggestions are displayed after successful analysis.

## US-07: Handle Errors

- [ ] Application displays an error when the backend cannot be reached.
- [ ] Backend returns an appropriate error response when AI processing fails.

---

# 6. Functional Requirements

### FR-01: Code Input

The system shall allow users to enter source code for analysis.

### FR-02: Code Analysis

The system shall send submitted code to the backend for AI-powered analysis.

### FR-03: Refactoring Suggestions

The system shall provide suggestions covering:

- Cleaner code
- Design patterns
- Optimization
- Naming improvements

### FR-04: Structured Response

The backend shall return the analysis in a structured JSON response.

### FR-05: Error Handling

The system shall provide feedback when analysis cannot be completed.

---

# 7. Out of Scope

The current version does not include:

- Automatic modification of the user's local files
- Automatic Git commits
- Automatic pull requests
- Automatic deployment
- Persistent storage of submitted source code
- Complete automated testing of arbitrary user programs Problem




- Multi-file analysis
